<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan CPC adjusts petrochemical prices.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CPC adjusts petrochemical prices.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp said it had adjusted product prices for March. The prices, annouced at the end of each month, apply retroactively to products sold during the month. (in U.S. dollars per tonne)</p>
<p>PRODUCT</p>
<p>						    March	 February</p>
<p>Ethylene					    569	   572</p>
<p>Polymer grade propylene			 453	   449</p>
<p>Chemical grade propylene			420	   416</p>
<p>Butadiene					   425	   448</p>
<p>Benzene					     305	   329</p>
<p>Paraxylene					  452	   455</p>
<p>Orthoxylene					 412	   409</p>
<p>Carbon black feedstock (per kilolitre)    101	   112</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
